While we're talking about confirmation, the one thing I don't like is the
use of the 'y' key to confirm. I know it's logical, it's just that if
you're moving diagonally up and to the left it's all too easy to
accidentally confirm the killing of your pet. I suppose I should be more
careful, really...

May as well throw in my opinion on pools - I think there should be some
kind of special equipment (snorkel?) which will let you breathe under water
- of course, you still won't be able to get _out_ with that plate mail
on... unless perhaps you levitate. If we're going to allow players into
pools, we should of course ruin scrolls and spellbooks, and dilute potions
(hehehe) unless they take precautions (waterproof sack, anyone?)

The moat should be too deep for snorkelling unless you're fairly unladen -
ring of water breathing? A spell? An aqualung? But, of course, you never
know whether there's a waterproof sack at the bottom with Stormbringer in
it ;-)

And, of course, if you're playing on a VT220 or an xterm there's no need to
complain about fountains looking like pools - simply set DECgraphics in
your NETHACKOPTIONS, and they will look VERY different indeed...

May your armour never rust.

